{"chunks": [{"chunk_id": "pilot-0", "document_id": "21cd91183448e089095c01795f01c0302dcac67e8094e46ecb0f8ce48d96bd3c", "filename": "maintenance_manual.md", "chunk_index": 0, "location": "", "content": "# P-Series Pump Maintenance Manual (excerpt)\n\n## Over-temperature shutdowns\nOver-temperature shutdowns on P-series pumps are typically caused by:\n1. Blocked cooling fins (dust accumulation in dusty environments)\n2. Bearing wear increasing friction load\n3. Low coolant level in closed-loop systems\n\n## Procedure: Bearing replacement (P-17 class)\n1. Depressurize and lock out the pump.\n2. Remove coupling guard and coupling.\n3. Extract bearing housing; inspect shaft for scoring.\n4. Fit new bearing (part BRG-4210), torque to 45 Nm.\n5. Reassemble, run at 50% load for 10 minutes, check temperature.\n\n## Escalation\nIf over-temperature shutdowns recur within 30 days of bearing replacement,\nescalate to the reliability engineer and check the coolant loop."}], "vectors": [[0.0636143907904625, 0.025882605463266373, -0.19371367990970612, -0.02419711835682392, 0.008826208300888538, 0.012944784015417099, 0.06960328668355942, 0.007984815165400505, 0.013338398188352585, -0.00044910621363669634, 0.02522556483745575, 0.020152660086750984, -0.00233282707631588, -0.020582789555191994, 0.03834971413016319, -0.014554188586771488, 0.013058255426585674, -0.05788085609674454, 0.003693757113069296, 0.007040570490062237, 0.016789309680461884, -0.07184216380119324, -0.06185949221253395, 0.02302442491054535, 0.04206770285964012, 0.02921922691166401, -0.018662229180336, 0.002180708572268486, -0.008257947862148285, -0.030798358842730522, 0.04677985608577728, -0.06182542443275452, -0.021608680486679077, -0.10161657631397247, -0.03907352685928345, -0.0351315513253212, 0.11798851191997528, 0.016840163618326187, 0.013257913291454315, -0.024493008852005005, 0.06930819898843765, -0.009620247408747673, 0.08530733734369278, -0.01663551852107048, 0.014137724414467812, 0.010535595007240772, 0.016